# Jenova, Ancient Calamity (1/5): "At the beginning of combat on your turn, put a number of +1/+1 counters equal to Jenova's power on up to one other target creature. That creature becomes a Mutant in addition
# to its other types." and "Whenever a Mutant you control dies during your turn, you draw cards equal to its power." Turn 1 Bot1 casts a Memnite and Jenova: at combat the Memnite (1/1) gets one counter
# and is a Mutant (2/2). Turn 3 it gets a second counter (3/3). Still on turn 3 a Lightning Bolt kills it and Bot1 draws exactly 3, the power it last had with both counters - not its base 1, not the 2
# of the first combat. Bot2's hand stays full (Jenova's own controller draws).

